Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Test Pods Failing to Start
Problem: Test pods remain in pending or error state.

Solution:

# Check pod events
kubectl describe pod -l "helm.sh/hook=test" --namespace helm-testing

# Check resource availability
kubectl top nodes
kubectl describe nodes

# Verify image availability
docker pull curlimages/curl:7.85.0
Issue 2: Service Connection Tests Failing
Problem: Connection tests cannot reach the service.

Solution:

# Check service endpoints
kubectl get endpoints --namespace helm-testing

# Verify pod readiness
kubectl get pods --namespace helm-testing -o wide

# Test service connectivity manually
kubectl run debug-pod --image=curlimages/curl:7.85.0 --rm -it --restart=Never --namespace helm-testing -- curl -f http://webapp-test:80/
Issue 3: RBAC Permission Issues
Problem: Test pods cannot access Kubernetes API.

Solution:

# Check service account
kubectl get serviceaccount --namespace helm-testing

# Verify role bindings
kubectl get rolebindings --namespace helm-testing

# Check permissions
kubectl auth can-i get deployments --as=system:serviceaccount:helm-testing:webapp-test-test-sa --namespace helm-testing
